WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:06.924
[theme music playing]

00:07.007 --> 00:09.885
[in English]
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:11.136 --> 00:14.723
♪ You're driving alone at night ♪

00:15.474 --> 00:20.395
♪ Deep in the silence
But it doesn't mean you're lost ♪

00:20.479 --> 00:23.690
♪ And I'll tell you what ♪

00:24.358 --> 00:26.485
♪ We're on the train ♪

00:27.319 --> 00:30.531
♪ I promise I'll be where you are ♪

00:31.865 --> 00:35.827
♪ If any thought is against you ♪

00:35.911 --> 00:39.498
♪ With you, I am starting over ♪

00:39.581 --> 00:43.377
♪ We're learning to walk again ♪

00:43.460 --> 00:45.420
OUR UNWRITTEN SEOUL

00:45.504 --> 00:46.755
[song concludes]

00:46.838 --> 00:49.174
[in Korean] The one with long hair?
Not the short-haired one?

00:49.258 --> 00:50.634
The one with long hair is Mi-ji.

00:50.717 --> 00:52.094
Wait, is that Mi-rae?

00:52.177 --> 00:54.555
- But you said you told Mi-ji--
- No, I didn't.

00:55.180 --> 00:57.224
I said I told the girl next door.

00:57.599 --> 00:59.851
So you didn't talk to Mi-ji about me?

00:59.935 --> 01:01.728
I can't tell if it was Mi-ji or Mi-rae.

01:01.812 --> 01:03.480
- [sighs]
- [Bun-hong] But that morning,

01:03.564 --> 01:07.901
the one I asked to help you
had long hair.

01:07.985 --> 01:08.902
TO MI-JI

01:08.986 --> 01:11.071
Don't worry,
it's easy to get them mixed up.

01:12.322 --> 01:13.865
Just get it right this time.

01:17.995 --> 01:19.371
[twin] Who is it?

01:21.290 --> 01:22.332
[soft music playing]

01:22.416 --> 01:25.419
[Mi-ji] There are some creepy stories
about identical beings.

01:28.422 --> 01:29.298
"Doppelgängers,"

01:29.381 --> 01:30.799
The Double,

01:30.882 --> 01:33.176
The Man in the Iron Mask,
and so on.

01:34.261 --> 01:35.804
[soft music continues]

01:44.938 --> 01:49.192
[Mi-ji] You'd think telling twins apart
would be easy enough.

01:50.402 --> 01:52.654
But without clues,
it's harder than you think.

01:54.156 --> 01:58.285
EPISODE 2
REVIEW AND REASSESS

01:58.702 --> 02:01.830
[music concludes]

02:03.165 --> 02:05.000
- [stylist] Excuse me.
- [client] Okay.

02:10.589 --> 02:12.841
- How do I look?
- Come on.

02:12.924 --> 02:14.801
You didn't bleach your hair?

02:14.885 --> 02:17.304
Let them think you dyed it.
I had to cut it, you know?

02:17.929 --> 02:20.641
Are you kidding? I got extensions.

02:21.558 --> 02:23.143
What the… [sighs]

02:25.020 --> 02:28.023
When did you even write this manual thing?

02:28.774 --> 02:29.983
While you were sleeping.

02:30.525 --> 02:32.736
I just wrote down the bare minimum.

02:32.819 --> 02:36.031
Didn't you say you were invisible?
How's this the bare minimum?

02:36.114 --> 02:37.199
[sighs]

02:37.282 --> 02:40.077
Is there anything I should know
before I go home?

02:40.869 --> 02:44.039
Nope, you already know how I live.

02:44.122 --> 02:47.709
Still, maybe some tips
on how you act around certain people?

02:47.793 --> 02:50.087
No one cares about me.

02:51.171 --> 02:52.798
[scoffs]

02:52.881 --> 02:54.174
[cell phone buzzing]

02:57.302 --> 02:59.805
LEE HO-SU

03:04.851 --> 03:06.311
BLOCK NUMBER

03:08.897 --> 03:11.149
I haven't missed the bus, have I? [pants]

03:11.775 --> 03:13.902
[driver] Bus eight leaves in five minutes.

03:13.985 --> 03:15.570
Time to board!

03:15.654 --> 03:16.822
[sighs]

03:19.074 --> 03:20.492
The passcode is our birthday.

03:20.575 --> 03:22.661
Gyeong-gu might call, but just ignore him.

03:25.247 --> 03:26.498
Are you sure this is okay?

03:26.581 --> 03:30.085
Oh, come on. This is about you
being okay, remember?

03:39.344 --> 03:42.389
Promise me you won't act up
and you'll lay low.

03:43.348 --> 03:45.892
If you go around
trying to fix my problems,

03:45.976 --> 03:47.227
I won't let it slide.

03:47.602 --> 03:51.314
Hey, you're back to the Mi-rae I know.

03:52.399 --> 03:53.442
I'm waiting.

03:53.984 --> 03:57.237
I promise. I'll just sit and keep quiet.

03:57.320 --> 03:58.321
Happy?

04:01.575 --> 04:03.785
[mouths] Keep your word.

04:04.202 --> 04:05.495
Okay, I get it.

04:08.081 --> 04:09.082
Bye.

04:11.293 --> 04:12.753
[cell phone buzzing]

04:15.714 --> 04:17.591
[Mi-ji]
"Seriously, don't do anything."

04:17.674 --> 04:18.759
[exhales]

04:27.350 --> 04:29.269
- [phone alarm ringing]
- Shoot.

04:33.732 --> 04:34.816
[alarm stops]

04:37.068 --> 04:38.487
[groans]

04:41.782 --> 04:44.075
[breathes deeply]

04:45.160 --> 04:46.203
[grunts]

04:48.288 --> 04:49.289
[sighs]

04:49.372 --> 04:51.958
- [breathes deeply]
- [soft daring music playing]

04:59.466 --> 05:00.717
[sighs heavily]

05:02.093 --> 05:05.013
Yesterday is over.
Tomorrow is yet to come.

05:05.096 --> 05:08.266
Today is yet unknown.

05:08.350 --> 05:09.434
Let's go.

05:12.979 --> 05:14.064
[door lock chirping]

05:16.024 --> 05:18.318
[soft daring music continues]

05:18.860 --> 05:22.364
DAY ONE

05:22.447 --> 05:23.490
[card reader beeps]

05:24.991 --> 05:27.953
[employee 1] Has this quarter's
policy funding schedule been released?

05:28.036 --> 05:30.413
[employee 2] Yes,
applications open next week.

05:30.497 --> 05:33.214
With the internal review period…

05:33.333 --> 05:35.670
BUILDING A BETTER TOMORROW,
TOGETHER IN FINANCE

05:39.214 --> 05:41.007
KOREA FINANCE
MANAGEMENT CORPORATION

05:41.216 --> 05:43.009
[overlapping chatter]

05:44.094 --> 05:45.345
[in English] Yeah, that's right.

05:45.428 --> 05:48.932
It's specifically designed
for investment professionals

05:49.015 --> 05:52.477
and current financial
institution representatives.

05:57.107 --> 05:58.233
[music concludes]

05:58.316 --> 06:01.570
[in Korean] We have a weekly meeting.
Go as early as you can.

06:01.653 --> 06:03.530
They don't tell me when it starts,

06:03.613 --> 06:05.907
so watch and follow everyone else in.

06:05.991 --> 06:08.493
I showed up an hour early, you jerks.

06:11.663 --> 06:13.248
- [Mi-ji] Hey.
- [drawer rattling]

06:14.666 --> 06:17.043
Looks like nobody's here yet.

06:17.127 --> 06:18.670
They're all in the meeting.

06:19.754 --> 06:20.964
Oh…

06:22.340 --> 06:23.633
[whispers] Darn it.

06:24.801 --> 06:26.136
[mouths] What the heck?

06:26.720 --> 06:29.139
[employee] Due to the rise
in insolvent enterprises, the PDF…

06:29.222 --> 06:31.266
[Mi-rae] If it's already started,
just sneak in.

06:31.349 --> 06:32.893
Try not to draw any attention.

06:32.976 --> 06:36.021
This PDF will most likely end up
just providing funding,

06:36.146 --> 06:38.607
- nothing… more…
- [door creaking slowly]

06:39.649 --> 06:41.151
[whispers] Shoot.

06:45.447 --> 06:46.615
- [Tae-gwan] Ms. Yu.
- Yes?

06:48.491 --> 06:49.534
Back from sick leave?

06:50.577 --> 06:52.120
[sighs] Yes.

06:52.203 --> 06:53.330
Sit.

06:54.080 --> 06:55.123
Okay.

06:55.707 --> 06:59.669
There won't be any seats.
Just sit in a chair by the window.

07:01.630 --> 07:02.797
Okay.

07:07.344 --> 07:10.055
[soft quirky music playing]

07:11.890 --> 07:12.807
[door opens]

07:12.891 --> 07:14.851
Coffee's… here.

07:28.615 --> 07:31.576
[Mi-rae] Don't forget, you're invisible.

07:31.660 --> 07:35.205
When they act like they can see you,
it's just to get a reaction.

07:35.288 --> 07:37.374
Even if it bothers you, don't react.

07:40.335 --> 07:42.671
No, I'm good. Let Ms. Yu have mine.

07:42.754 --> 07:45.465
I guess you forgot hers
because she's been on sick leave.

07:45.548 --> 07:47.008
Go ahead, drink up. You too.

07:48.677 --> 07:50.011
[employee chuckles softly]

07:51.846 --> 07:53.264
Let's continue.

07:53.348 --> 07:54.516
Yes…

07:55.100 --> 07:57.852
So in conclusion,
with the existing PDF we have…

07:57.936 --> 08:00.480
[Mi-rae] There's a ton of jargon
and acronyms in these meetings.

08:00.563 --> 08:01.690
You won't understand much.

08:01.773 --> 08:05.527
But they won't ask for your opinion,
so just sit tight--

08:05.610 --> 08:07.487
Senior Specialist Yu Mi-rae,
what's your take?

08:07.570 --> 08:09.322
- [music concludes]
- What?

08:09.406 --> 08:12.283
Didn't you take that seat
so you could say something?

08:12.367 --> 08:15.954
You're the most PC
and morally upright person here,

08:17.038 --> 08:19.582
so let's hear your thoughts
on ESG management.

08:20.417 --> 08:21.793
ESG…

08:21.876 --> 08:27.340
Well, if you ask me,
I think ESG management is

08:27.424 --> 08:29.342
very important,

08:29.426 --> 08:31.594
- and…
- [tense quirky music playing]

08:32.137 --> 08:34.264
…there's definitely
a lot of weight to it--

08:34.347 --> 08:37.559
So, how should we set

08:37.642 --> 08:40.145
those all-important ESG KPIs?

08:40.687 --> 08:43.106
K, K-pop… K?

08:43.189 --> 08:44.399
Oh, K!

08:44.482 --> 08:47.068
K… K…

08:47.152 --> 08:48.445
[Tae-gwan] That's enough.

08:48.945 --> 08:51.948
Why put her on the spot like that
when we're short on time?

08:53.575 --> 08:56.703
Anyway, it's good to hear
your voice again, Ms. Yu.

08:56.786 --> 08:58.872
- Hmm. Yes.
- Let's wrap up.

09:07.213 --> 09:09.883
[employee] I can't believe
you actually answered that.

09:09.966 --> 09:12.719
- [music fades]
- You take everything so literally.

09:12.802 --> 09:14.220
That's why you misunderstand people.

09:14.304 --> 09:16.473
I just feel bad for Mr. Park.

09:17.849 --> 09:19.809
He shouldn't have looked out for her.

09:27.317 --> 09:30.361
[whispers] Those bullies…

09:30.445 --> 09:31.613
[door closes]

09:31.696 --> 09:32.947
[clears throat]

09:46.586 --> 09:50.048
- [male voice] Ms. Yu. I mean, Mi-rae.
- [eerie music playing]

09:53.885 --> 09:56.012
[music intensifies]

09:57.055 --> 09:58.139
[voice 1] That's Yu Mi-rae.

09:58.223 --> 10:00.308
- [voice 2] Why is she here?
- [voice 3] She's got nerve.

10:00.391 --> 10:02.685
- [voice 4 laughs] She did it.
- [voice 5] She's so shameless.

10:02.769 --> 10:04.729
- [voice 6] Right. It was her.
- [voice 7] No way.

10:04.813 --> 10:07.440
- [voice 6] She's brazen.
- [voice 8] How funny.

10:07.524 --> 10:08.733
[voice 9] Gosh!

10:08.817 --> 10:12.862
[eerie overlapping chatter and laughter]

10:15.657 --> 10:16.866
[chatter stops abruptly]

10:16.950 --> 10:18.451
[female voice] Ms. Yu Mi-rae?

10:24.165 --> 10:25.708
- [gasps]
- [music stops abruptly]

10:33.091 --> 10:34.676
[slow suspenseful music playing]

10:34.759 --> 10:35.802
You…

10:37.345 --> 10:38.930
You're back from Seoul…

10:41.724 --> 10:43.893
Mom…

10:49.566 --> 10:50.859
I mean…

10:52.026 --> 10:53.486
Did you dye your hair?

10:54.195 --> 10:55.446
What?

10:55.530 --> 10:56.614
[music turns intriguing]

10:56.698 --> 10:57.782
Yeah.

10:57.866 --> 10:59.742
It looks way better.

10:59.826 --> 11:02.745
Good God. It was hard to look at before!

11:02.829 --> 11:05.165
- [music fades]
- You finally did the right thing.

11:05.248 --> 11:07.834
It looks great. Let's go eat.

11:08.251 --> 11:09.836
That was a nice surprise!

11:09.919 --> 11:12.046
[breathes deeply]

11:14.883 --> 11:17.844
Did Mi-rae finish all the kimchi I sent?

11:18.428 --> 11:20.805
[Mi-ji] No, she left quite a lot.

11:21.472 --> 11:24.392
I don't think you need
to send her food anymore.

11:25.018 --> 11:28.521
She hardly eats at home,
so it just sits there--

11:28.605 --> 11:29.731
I know.

11:31.482 --> 11:33.318
She's always been a picky eater.

11:33.401 --> 11:36.070
You know that?
Then why do you send it to her?

11:36.571 --> 11:39.115
It's the only thing I can do
to ease my guilt.

11:40.116 --> 11:42.327
She sends me money every month.

11:42.827 --> 11:44.829
The least I can do is send her some food.

11:44.913 --> 11:46.080
[Ok-hui slurps]

11:47.290 --> 11:49.626
So it's out of guilt?

11:50.376 --> 11:51.836
Because you feel bad?

11:52.545 --> 11:53.588
Jeez.

11:55.131 --> 11:57.300
You wouldn't know guilt if it hit you.

11:57.800 --> 11:59.552
I mean, gosh.

12:00.303 --> 12:02.138
Why aren't you answering your phone?

12:02.931 --> 12:04.974
- What do you mean?
- Grandma's caregiver called.

12:05.058 --> 12:07.268
She said she couldn't reach you.

12:08.937 --> 12:10.813
She's out for a few days. Family stuff.

12:10.897 --> 12:11.981
2 NEW MESSAGES

12:12.982 --> 12:15.318
You'll go even if I
tell you not to, right?

12:15.401 --> 12:16.402
Go where?

12:16.486 --> 12:19.239
The hospital.
You'll visit Grandma, won't you?

12:20.490 --> 12:22.492
[Mi-ji] I only have one condition.

12:22.575 --> 12:24.410
Visit Grandma twice a week.

12:24.911 --> 12:27.580
What? Grandma will know right away.

12:27.664 --> 12:29.999
No excuses. Twice a week.

12:33.378 --> 12:34.587
I'm busy.

12:34.671 --> 12:36.547
[scoffs] Busy doing what?
You're unemployed.

12:40.343 --> 12:41.511
I have work.

12:44.389 --> 12:46.683
[Se-jin] Come to the strawberry farm
by two o'clock.

12:46.766 --> 12:48.226
Changhwa Farm.

12:51.312 --> 12:54.857
I'd rather work on the farm
than get caught right away.

12:55.191 --> 12:56.985
START - END

12:57.068 --> 12:58.319
3 KM, 48 MIN ON FOOT

12:58.403 --> 13:00.947
[Mi-rae] What? Three kilometers?

13:06.327 --> 13:08.288
[serene music playing]

13:08.871 --> 13:10.748
[whimpering]

13:10.832 --> 13:12.667
- [tire screeching]
- Oh, no!

13:12.750 --> 13:15.336
DUSON-RI SENIOR CENTER

13:15.420 --> 13:16.713
GYEONG-GU MART

13:17.630 --> 13:20.300
Hey, Mi-ji! Did you dye your hair?

13:21.217 --> 13:22.302
Yu Mi-ji!

13:22.385 --> 13:26.180
What's going on? Is she drunk?

13:27.015 --> 13:28.016
[Mi-ji] Gosh, no!

13:28.099 --> 13:31.519
[Myeong-gap] That's not biking.
That's a crime on wheels.

13:31.602 --> 13:32.937
CHANGHWA FARM

13:33.021 --> 13:34.230
[whimpers]

13:34.939 --> 13:38.443
[Mi-rae yelling indistinctly]

13:40.653 --> 13:41.654
Oh!

13:47.160 --> 13:49.912
- [panting]
- [music concludes]

13:49.996 --> 13:51.247
Hi.

13:51.956 --> 13:54.167
I'm Yu Mi-ji. I got your text.

13:55.043 --> 13:56.252
[soft quirky music playing]

13:56.336 --> 13:57.378
DUSON-RI YOUTH ASSOCIATION

13:57.462 --> 13:59.964
You were looking for some help?

14:00.048 --> 14:02.008
Isn't this Changhwa Farm?

14:02.967 --> 14:06.471
[chuckling] What's with this act?

14:06.554 --> 14:09.849
It's only been a few days,
and you're playing pretend?

14:09.932 --> 14:12.310
If you're that bored, tie these up.

14:12.393 --> 14:14.395
[chuckles nervously] Okay.

14:14.896 --> 14:16.022
[chuckles]

14:17.106 --> 14:18.358
Very good.

14:18.441 --> 14:21.652
You came to play along with a crazy guy
for 200,000 won?

14:21.736 --> 14:24.655
He's been talking about
planting a new kind of strawberry

14:24.739 --> 14:26.532
when the season's long gone.

14:27.909 --> 14:29.744
What will you use after you've tilled?

14:29.827 --> 14:31.454
Pipes or heating wires?

14:34.374 --> 14:35.375
Pardon?

14:35.458 --> 14:38.086
Quit the act.
I mean for the temperature control.

14:39.128 --> 14:40.963
Oh, temperature…

14:41.047 --> 14:43.049
[Se-jin] Why all the questions?

14:44.300 --> 14:45.343
Tell me.

14:46.135 --> 14:47.637
- Why?
- [music concludes]

14:47.720 --> 14:51.682
[Se-jin] And you should be asking
the owner about that stuff.

14:52.683 --> 14:54.268
Did you get the text?

14:54.352 --> 14:55.770
Oh, yes.

14:58.564 --> 15:01.192
Is the owner in there?

15:01.275 --> 15:02.944
He's right here.

15:03.945 --> 15:05.488
[gentle music playing]

15:05.571 --> 15:09.117
There are three greenhouses,
but we're only tilling this one for now.

15:09.200 --> 15:10.493
Uh… [grunts]

15:13.996 --> 15:15.081
There.

15:17.041 --> 15:18.209
[blows]

15:22.755 --> 15:26.342
Everyone's into smart farming these days,

15:26.426 --> 15:28.302
but we use terrace cultivation.

15:29.095 --> 15:31.139
What does that mean?

15:33.099 --> 15:34.267
We use soil?

15:35.852 --> 15:37.103
Right.

15:37.186 --> 15:38.604
You're pretty smart.

15:39.897 --> 15:41.816
What else does it mean?

15:43.109 --> 15:45.528
- It's organic.
- [music concludes]

15:45.611 --> 15:47.822
Maybe you heard from
the Youth Association President,

15:47.905 --> 15:49.615
but last year's harvest was a bust.

15:49.699 --> 15:53.578
I listened to everyone in the village,
and it all went sideways.

15:53.661 --> 15:56.164
But now, I just need to listen
to you, Mi-hee.

15:57.123 --> 15:59.709
It's Mi-ji. Yu Mi-ji.

15:59.792 --> 16:01.210
Sorry.

16:01.294 --> 16:03.379
Anyway, now that we've got
a veteran on board,

16:03.463 --> 16:06.591
I'm going to run things my way this year.

16:07.133 --> 16:09.469
We'll get things going
at the end of the month.

16:09.886 --> 16:11.012
That's all.

16:12.930 --> 16:14.724
Then what should I do now?

16:16.225 --> 16:17.727
Well, for now…

16:18.603 --> 16:20.188
whatever you want, Min-ji.

16:20.980 --> 16:24.317
Do what you think is best
for the first week.

16:26.319 --> 16:28.738
Aren't you expecting too much
from a part-timer?

16:28.821 --> 16:30.990
I hired a partner, not a part-timer.

16:32.408 --> 16:34.660
If there's nothing to do,
you can just relax.

16:34.744 --> 16:36.496
You'll get paid daily after work.

16:37.079 --> 16:40.374
Oh! You can set your own hours.

16:40.458 --> 16:41.626
[clicks tongue]

16:43.794 --> 16:44.962
Good luck!

16:46.005 --> 16:47.131
Jeez.

16:48.382 --> 16:51.844
[vocalizing playful tune]

16:53.304 --> 16:55.890
This "abuse of power" crap.

16:55.973 --> 16:59.185
Now I can't even breathe
without being accused of abuse.

16:59.268 --> 17:02.188
Legally speaking,
it was more than just breathing.

17:03.022 --> 17:06.108
Our priority should be to avoid a lawsuit,

17:06.192 --> 17:07.401
so let's try to settle first.

17:07.485 --> 17:08.945
Settle?

17:09.028 --> 17:10.154
No way.

17:10.655 --> 17:13.950
You charge twice as much as other lawyers,

17:14.116 --> 17:16.744
and your brilliant idea
is to just pay him off?

17:16.827 --> 17:18.788
It's best to offer something now,

17:19.372 --> 17:21.874
or it'll end up costing
a lot more down the road.

17:22.667 --> 17:24.335
Don't give him a dime. Just win!

17:24.418 --> 17:26.045
I'd like that too,

17:27.129 --> 17:29.549
but you're still on probation.

17:29.632 --> 17:32.927
You said it was just a few hits,
so I assumed it was nothing serious.

17:33.010 --> 17:35.513
But you broke both his legs
and expect it to just go away?

17:35.596 --> 17:37.139
Jeez.

17:38.099 --> 17:41.185
Just because you're both damaged goods,

17:41.269 --> 17:42.645
you're covering for him?

17:43.396 --> 17:44.438
[laptop slams shut]

17:44.939 --> 17:46.357
What's your problem?

17:46.941 --> 17:48.317
[pensive music playing]

17:48.401 --> 17:50.361
It was June 15, 2020.

17:51.529 --> 17:52.738
What was?

17:52.822 --> 17:54.740
Mr. Kim Seung-yong

17:54.824 --> 17:58.536
got his license suspended
for 100 days for DUI.

17:59.036 --> 18:02.039
And he interviewed for the driver job
on September 15, 2020.

18:04.709 --> 18:06.210
Wait, then…

18:06.294 --> 18:08.254
While his license was still suspended…

18:09.630 --> 18:11.215
he started working as your driver.

18:14.093 --> 18:17.722
We might be able to win this
without offering any payment.

18:18.347 --> 18:20.933
Get that settlement
or whatever it is done.

18:21.017 --> 18:23.477
Don't drag it out
to squeeze more money out of me.

18:24.103 --> 18:27.857
The less he gets,
the more you earn your keep. Got it?

18:27.940 --> 18:32.028
We earn our keep
by keeping you out of jail, sir.

18:32.111 --> 18:33.112
[shouts] What?

18:33.195 --> 18:34.905
If the fees are too much,

18:34.989 --> 18:37.199
I'd be happy to refer you
to another lawyer.

18:37.283 --> 18:39.869
They are all good at what they do.

18:41.287 --> 18:43.205
Please take care.

18:44.206 --> 18:45.458
[clears throat]

18:52.673 --> 18:54.133
[music concludes]

18:54.216 --> 18:56.594
Gosh, for someone who's loaded,

18:56.677 --> 18:59.180
he never stops
complaining about having to pay.

19:00.806 --> 19:01.974
I'm sorry.

19:02.475 --> 19:03.601
What for?

19:03.684 --> 19:05.561
For not telling you sooner.

19:05.645 --> 19:07.897
I found evidence
that his license was suspended,

19:07.980 --> 19:10.191
but I wasn't sure whether to say anything.

19:10.816 --> 19:12.568
And you said it

19:12.652 --> 19:15.279
because you felt sorry for me
over the "damaged goods" comment?

19:15.363 --> 19:17.823
Not at all. If anything, I…

19:17.907 --> 19:21.911
I wasn’t trying to undermine
anyone’s capability due to a disability--

19:21.994 --> 19:22.995
Ho-su.

19:24.455 --> 19:26.666
What do you say in situations like this?

19:28.459 --> 19:31.921
I… just wanted to win.

19:32.004 --> 19:33.339
There you go.

19:33.422 --> 19:35.299
Come on, I'll whip up something good.

19:35.841 --> 19:37.718
[blender whirring]

19:41.847 --> 19:43.641
[Chung-gu] What was it again?

19:43.724 --> 19:46.435
I've uploaded the draft
of the Youngho Holdings opinion letter

19:46.519 --> 19:48.396
and the Derma Beauty equity report.

19:48.479 --> 19:50.189
For the Eco Energy
industrial accident case,

19:50.272 --> 19:51.899
I'll go with
the ministry's interpretation.

19:51.982 --> 19:54.151
Good. Refer to the Jinsu Group case.

19:54.777 --> 19:56.195
All done.

19:56.278 --> 19:57.279
Bottoms up.

19:58.447 --> 19:59.865
Is this safe to drink?

19:59.949 --> 20:01.492
You don't know Buzz Boost?

20:01.575 --> 20:03.911
Back in college,
people used to pay me for it.

20:03.994 --> 20:05.329
They all passed the bar.

20:05.413 --> 20:06.831
Their health took a hit, though.

20:13.754 --> 20:16.382
[exhales loudly] Now I'm wide awake.

20:16.465 --> 20:18.801
- Let me…
- [exhales]

20:20.553 --> 20:23.305
You are going to KFMC this week, right?

20:23.389 --> 20:25.099
Yes, for the advisory meeting.

20:25.808 --> 20:28.436
By the way, about the whistleblowing case…

20:28.519 --> 20:30.396
You can drop that.

20:30.479 --> 20:31.897
It's been handled.

20:32.898 --> 20:34.942
Already? I haven't started investigating.

20:35.025 --> 20:36.068
YU MI-RAE

20:36.152 --> 20:38.612
Looks like
they took care of it internally.

20:42.366 --> 20:43.367
What?

20:43.993 --> 20:46.162
Are you worried
because she was a classmate?

20:46.704 --> 20:48.289
No, not at all.

20:48.372 --> 20:49.415
Good.

20:49.957 --> 20:53.169
Overthinking only gets
in the way in this job.

20:53.252 --> 20:54.253
Understood?

20:56.297 --> 20:57.214
[Chung-gu exhales]

21:05.598 --> 21:07.850
[quirky music playing]

21:11.395 --> 21:12.480
I'll head out first--

21:12.563 --> 21:14.148
[Mi-rae] Don't say goodbye.

21:16.233 --> 21:17.485
[clears throat]

21:23.699 --> 21:25.951
She's acting odd today, right?

21:28.871 --> 21:31.540
YOUR PARTNER TO SUCCESS
HANJIN BANK

21:32.208 --> 21:33.250
[sighs]

21:33.334 --> 21:34.274
200,000 WON

21:39.298 --> 21:42.593
[Mi-rae]
Sorry, but I can't keep working like this…

21:42.676 --> 21:43.928
[cell phone buzzing]

21:46.055 --> 21:47.389
[Mi-ji] Made it through the day.

21:48.432 --> 21:49.892
[Mi-rae] How was everything?

21:50.851 --> 21:51.977
[Mi-ji] Too easy.

21:52.937 --> 21:54.855
What if it's really easy,

21:55.689 --> 21:57.650
and I'm just not cut out for it?

21:57.733 --> 21:59.401
SORRY, BUT…

22:00.444 --> 22:01.403
[video game chime]

22:01.737 --> 22:02.696
[cash register dinging]

22:02.780 --> 22:05.449
Of course it's too easy. All I do is sit.

22:06.200 --> 22:09.495
Gosh, I could do this for a year.

22:10.496 --> 22:12.665
DAY TWO

22:12.748 --> 22:14.416
[mouse wheel rattling]

22:14.500 --> 22:16.252
BUILDING AN OPEN-SOURCE
AI SYSTEM IN FINANCE

22:16.335 --> 22:18.045
[quirky music continues]

22:19.547 --> 22:23.509
[mouse wheel rattling, echoing]

22:24.760 --> 22:25.928
[Se-jin] Mi-rim.

22:26.011 --> 22:26.971
Shoot.

22:27.054 --> 22:29.181
[quirky music continues]

22:29.682 --> 22:30.975
What do you want for lunch?

22:34.436 --> 22:35.437
You don't want to talk?

22:35.521 --> 22:37.796
DAY THREE

22:37.940 --> 22:39.483
[quirky music continues]

22:44.572 --> 22:45.698
[chuckles]

22:49.159 --> 22:51.904
DAY FOUR

22:51.996 --> 22:53.706
[quirky music continues]

23:04.592 --> 23:05.759
[Mi-ji] Mm.

23:10.431 --> 23:12.725
- [music concludes]
- [team leader] What's the cafeteria menu?

23:12.808 --> 23:13.726
[employee 1] Army stew.

23:13.809 --> 23:14.727
A WEEK LATER

23:14.810 --> 23:16.520
- Is that it?
- Can't we go out for meat?

23:16.604 --> 23:19.523
- [employee 2] That sounds great.
- [employee 3] To a restaurant?

23:27.615 --> 23:28.866
Gosh.

23:29.450 --> 23:31.201
This is brutal.

23:31.285 --> 23:33.370
How did Mi-rae survive this?

23:34.288 --> 23:35.998
My whole body's stiff.

23:36.081 --> 23:37.333
[groaning]

23:39.168 --> 23:40.085
[grunts]

23:40.586 --> 23:41.837
Gosh.

23:41.921 --> 23:44.465
[intriguing music playing]

23:54.475 --> 23:56.602
- Feeling uncomfortable?
- Not at all.

23:56.685 --> 23:59.605
Must be tough for a hotshot
to sit around doing nothing.

24:00.356 --> 24:01.690
- No.
- Come on.

24:01.774 --> 24:03.484
It's written all over your face.

24:04.443 --> 24:07.237
If you'd like,
I could give you a simple task.

24:08.906 --> 24:11.784
[breathes deeply]

24:11.867 --> 24:12.952
Actually, no.

24:13.494 --> 24:15.454
With the way things are these days,

24:15.537 --> 24:18.040
I'll just get blamed later
for sending someone out.

24:18.958 --> 24:20.584
Forget I said anything.

24:20.668 --> 24:22.920
Sending me out, you said?

24:23.003 --> 24:23.963
[music concludes]

24:24.922 --> 24:28.509
You heard our team's handling
the new HQ site, right?

24:30.552 --> 24:33.138
It's a confidential project,
so we're keeping the team small,

24:33.222 --> 24:34.640
but progress is slow.

24:34.723 --> 24:37.643
If I give the busy ones more work,

24:37.726 --> 24:39.603
something's bound to fall through.

24:39.687 --> 24:42.272
[team leader] Director Choi,
just give me a little more time.

24:42.356 --> 24:44.233
Why trust Yu Mi-rae with--

24:44.316 --> 24:46.860
[inhales deeply] Mr. Shin.

24:48.028 --> 24:52.658
What if Ms. Yu files a complaint
about being sidelined?

24:52.741 --> 24:55.202
[intriguing music playing]

24:55.285 --> 24:59.665
PLANNING COORDINATION DEPT.
DIRECTOR CHOI TAE-GWAN

25:06.672 --> 25:07.881
Choose wisely.

25:08.632 --> 25:11.802
By accepting confidential information,
you're implicitly agreeing.

25:12.678 --> 25:16.390
If you're uncertain,
it might be better to just stay put.

25:29.862 --> 25:31.780
You saw the internal email, right?

25:32.281 --> 25:35.034
Performance reviews
are much stricter this year,

25:35.117 --> 25:36.869
so you'll have to work hard.

25:36.952 --> 25:38.579
I'm sure you'll manage.

25:38.662 --> 25:39.663
You can go.

25:39.747 --> 25:40.956
Okay.

25:44.251 --> 25:46.253
[mouse clicking]

25:50.841 --> 25:53.886
RECRUITING FOR EXTERNAL BRANCH POSITIONS

25:55.888 --> 25:58.140
[employee 1] Did you see the opening
at the Childal branch?

25:58.223 --> 25:59.308
[employee 2] Again?

25:59.391 --> 26:01.685
Didn't someone from accounting
get sent there last month?

26:01.769 --> 26:03.062
That one didn't last a month?

26:03.145 --> 26:07.149
[employee 1] Apparently, the assignments
will be based on performance reviews.

26:07.232 --> 26:09.318
Jeez, is this Russian roulette or what?

26:09.401 --> 26:10.569
[employee 2 sighs]

26:10.652 --> 26:13.864
Wait, you got that job?

26:13.947 --> 26:15.157
[music concludes]

26:15.240 --> 26:16.992
Guess you're off to Childal now.

26:17.951 --> 26:18.994
What?

26:20.037 --> 26:21.371
CONFIDENTIAL

26:22.331 --> 26:23.415
[daring music playing]

26:23.499 --> 26:24.750
CHILDAL BRANCH: ONE POSITION

26:24.833 --> 26:26.835
SELECTED BY PERFORMANCE REVIEW
IF NO ONE APPLIES

26:26.919 --> 26:28.420
[Mi-ji] Childal?

26:30.714 --> 26:32.758
[Gyeong-min]
We've nearly secured all the land,

26:32.841 --> 26:35.010
but there's one prime spot still.

26:36.804 --> 26:40.099
It's registered as Rosa Restaurant,
but there's no sign, so it's hard to find.

26:40.182 --> 26:41.517
ROSA RESTAURANT

26:41.600 --> 26:43.102
She's a stubborn old lady.

26:43.769 --> 26:45.771
For now, just hand her the proposal.

26:47.314 --> 26:49.108
- [exhales]
- [music swells, concludes]

26:49.191 --> 26:52.694
I know how to handle older folks. Hmm.

26:55.864 --> 26:59.326
CHICKEN GIBLET STEW

26:59.409 --> 27:01.078
Oh, hello.

27:01.161 --> 27:02.830
- Do you know the owner…
- [customer] I swear!

27:02.913 --> 27:05.499
I only had one shot. Just one!

27:05.582 --> 27:06.708
[Mi-ji gasps]

27:06.792 --> 27:08.544
That is one shot too many.

27:09.086 --> 27:11.255
What are you doing? You guys get out too.

27:11.338 --> 27:14.424
Hey, not us! He drank it all by himself.

27:14.508 --> 27:15.717
You little…

27:16.301 --> 27:18.303
Fine, I'll leave.

27:18.387 --> 27:20.222
Screw this place.

27:20.305 --> 27:22.099
Don't expect me to come back.

27:22.182 --> 27:23.392
[gargles, spits]

27:23.475 --> 27:25.227
- [bystander] Ugh, what the--
- [customer] Jeez!

27:25.310 --> 27:26.854
[bystander] No wonder he got kicked out.

27:26.937 --> 27:27.980
[customer] Hey!

27:30.816 --> 27:32.234
What?

27:32.317 --> 27:33.318
[chuckles]

27:34.069 --> 27:36.405
Do you serve solo diners?

27:36.488 --> 27:37.614
No, I don't.

27:37.698 --> 27:40.450
Then I'll order for two.

27:41.618 --> 27:42.995
[sighs]

27:43.078 --> 27:46.165
Perfect timing!
Make that two. I'll eat with her.

27:46.248 --> 27:48.458
- Let's share a table.
- What?

27:52.379 --> 27:53.380
Oh.

27:53.463 --> 27:55.799
[customers chattering]

27:57.843 --> 27:59.678
NO ALCOHOL ALLOWED

28:07.603 --> 28:09.897
[stranger] You can't order two servings
if you're alone.

28:09.980 --> 28:12.941
It's not just about the portion.
That's just the rule here.

28:13.025 --> 28:17.487
And they only serve chicken giblet soup,
so don't bother asking for anything else.

28:17.571 --> 28:20.490
You saw the sign earlier, right?
No alcohol allowed.

28:20.574 --> 28:22.075
No takeout and no delivery either.

28:22.159 --> 28:24.411
- [thrilling music playing]
- [knife thudding]

28:25.454 --> 28:27.080
- [stranger] Don't stare at her.
- Sorry?

28:27.164 --> 28:29.833
[stranger] You'll get yelled at
if you make eye contact.

28:29.917 --> 28:31.335
Anyway, this works out.

28:31.418 --> 28:34.254
I've been waiting over 30 minutes
hoping someone would share a table.

28:34.338 --> 28:35.714
My friend couldn't make it.

28:35.797 --> 28:37.633
[Mi-ji] Isn't that too much hassle?

28:37.716 --> 28:39.927
[stranger]
You'll understand once you try it.

28:40.469 --> 28:42.095
Here it comes.

28:44.223 --> 28:46.308
- [music concludes]
- [customers chattering]

28:51.855 --> 28:53.482
[stranger] Go on, try it.

28:59.363 --> 29:01.281
[gasps] Mm!

29:02.032 --> 29:03.283
Wow.

29:03.367 --> 29:05.327
So that's what it tastes like.

29:05.410 --> 29:07.287
Here, let me serve you some.

29:12.000 --> 29:13.752
- See you.
- [Mi-ji] Okay.

29:13.835 --> 29:15.420
Ma'am.

29:15.504 --> 29:17.422
- That was amazing.
- [cash register dinging]

29:17.506 --> 29:19.758
I'd never had chicken giblet soup before,

29:19.841 --> 29:22.761
but it's so delicious,
and there's no weird smell at all.

29:23.303 --> 29:24.388
Thank you.

29:24.888 --> 29:28.517
I was so busy eating
that I forgot to introduce myself.

29:28.600 --> 29:32.187
I'm Yu Mi-rae from Korea Finance
Management Corporation.

29:35.232 --> 29:38.277
You got a call from us
a while back, correct?

29:38.360 --> 29:40.112
About the new HQ site.

29:41.655 --> 29:43.532
So today,

29:44.241 --> 29:47.911
I just wanted to hand over
some documents and explain…

29:48.787 --> 29:51.456
All right… Should we talk outside?

29:51.999 --> 29:54.793
Ma'am, this is the exit…

29:54.876 --> 29:56.420
Wait. Just a moment.

29:56.503 --> 30:00.257
I'm just here to drop off the paperwork…

30:00.340 --> 30:01.258
[yelps]

30:03.176 --> 30:07.097
I'm not selling, so don't come back.

30:07.180 --> 30:09.933
[dramatic quirky music playing]

30:14.813 --> 30:15.856
[sighs]

30:15.939 --> 30:17.983
[music concludes]

30:18.066 --> 30:18.984
[grunts]

30:26.325 --> 30:27.326
Hey!

30:28.452 --> 30:29.578
There.

30:31.747 --> 30:33.081
Thank you.

30:36.084 --> 30:39.421
I've been here a week today.

30:39.504 --> 30:40.589
Already?

30:41.173 --> 30:42.507
Wow, time flies.

30:42.591 --> 30:44.801
Since the probation period is over,

30:44.885 --> 30:47.888
could you let me know
if you plan to give me some work,

30:47.971 --> 30:49.306
or if you'd prefer I leave?

30:49.389 --> 30:50.599
One more week.

30:50.682 --> 30:51.683
Pardon?

30:51.767 --> 30:53.560
Do whatever you want for another week.

30:54.770 --> 30:56.188
- But…
- What do you think?

30:56.772 --> 30:59.232
Does this look
like a sweet potato or a potato?

30:59.316 --> 31:01.360
I really want a potato right now.

31:01.443 --> 31:03.904
What should I do? Jeez.

31:03.987 --> 31:05.113
[exhales]

31:06.073 --> 31:08.367
[Mi-ji] She listed all the snacks
in the break room,

31:08.450 --> 31:11.703
but nothing about how to
persuade property owners?

31:11.787 --> 31:13.038
Darn it.

31:14.331 --> 31:16.041
What is this?

31:16.917 --> 31:17.793
[gasps]

31:17.876 --> 31:19.127
She prepared all this too?

31:19.211 --> 31:22.672
Gosh, I should've read this earlier.

31:24.466 --> 31:26.218
[suspenseful music playing]

31:26.301 --> 31:27.177
What the heck?

31:27.260 --> 31:28.720
[Mi-rae] Team Leader Shin Gyeong-min.

31:28.804 --> 31:29.930
[Mi-ji] He's married.

31:30.013 --> 31:33.517
[Mi-rae] He's probably the most annoying,
but basically a puppet of the number one.

31:33.600 --> 31:35.102
He's number two on my stay-away list.

31:35.185 --> 31:36.186
He's number two?

31:36.269 --> 31:38.814
- Then who's number one?
- [Mi-rae] Director Choi Tae-gwan.

31:38.897 --> 31:40.774
Director Choi Tae-gwan.

31:41.316 --> 31:44.069
I guess you forgot hers
because she's been on sick leave.

31:44.152 --> 31:45.153
Go ahead, drink up.

31:45.237 --> 31:47.781
Must be tough for a hotshot
to sit around doing nothing.

31:47.864 --> 31:48.865
Choose wisely.

31:48.949 --> 31:51.535
By accepting confidential information,
you're implicitly agreeing.

31:51.618 --> 31:53.328
[suspenseful music continues]

31:53.995 --> 31:58.667
[Mi-rae] Don't be fooled by his kindness.
He's number one on the stay-away list.

31:58.750 --> 32:00.043
[gasps]

32:00.127 --> 32:02.754
Damn it. Was it all a setup?

32:02.838 --> 32:04.256
[shouting] What do I do now?

32:04.339 --> 32:07.592
[breathes deeply]

32:07.676 --> 32:09.386
[music builds, concludes]

32:09.469 --> 32:11.054
HOW TO CONVINCE LANDOWNERS

32:12.973 --> 32:14.349
Jeez, please.

32:14.433 --> 32:16.601
HOW TO WIN OVER LANDOWNERS
FOR REDEVELOPMENT

32:16.685 --> 32:18.019
[breathes heavily]

32:18.103 --> 32:20.981
Mi-ji, calm down. It's not over yet.

32:21.064 --> 32:24.401
Just pull yourself together
and let's make this happen.

32:25.444 --> 32:26.778
[cell phone buzzing]

32:26.862 --> 32:27.863
MESSAGE FROM MI-JI

32:27.946 --> 32:30.115
[gasps] Oh my gosh! What the…

32:30.198 --> 32:31.783
Is she watching me?

32:31.867 --> 32:33.160
That scared me.

32:36.288 --> 32:37.247
What?

32:37.330 --> 32:39.374
[Mi-rae] What do you do
during the farming off-season?

32:39.458 --> 32:40.584
Off-season?

32:41.001 --> 32:42.294
[cell phone buzzes]

32:44.421 --> 32:45.547
[Mi-ji] I just chill.

32:45.630 --> 32:47.007
- [sighs]
- [video game chime]

32:47.090 --> 32:48.091
[cash register dinging]

32:48.175 --> 32:49.718
DAY EIGHT

32:49.801 --> 32:51.386
[quirky music playing]

32:51.470 --> 32:52.429
[grunts]

32:53.680 --> 32:54.848
[door bell chimes]

32:55.640 --> 32:58.435
[quirky music continues]

33:02.147 --> 33:04.191
[cow moos in distance]

33:11.364 --> 33:13.074
[chuckles nervously]

33:13.158 --> 33:14.534
- [music builds, concludes]
- [groans]

33:14.618 --> 33:16.495
Ma'am, I'm sorry. Wait!

33:17.120 --> 33:19.122
[dramatic quirky music playing]

33:19.206 --> 33:20.415
- [Mi-rae] I…
- Shh.

33:22.751 --> 33:23.793
Oh my!

33:24.419 --> 33:25.545
False alarm.

33:28.924 --> 33:30.300
[cell phone buzzing]

33:32.427 --> 33:33.887
[Mi-rae] Is everything okay?

33:34.471 --> 33:36.014
[Mi-ji] Of course.

33:36.515 --> 33:38.433
DAY NINE

33:38.517 --> 33:40.519
[dramatic quirky music continues]

33:44.439 --> 33:46.441
Ma'am, please…

33:46.525 --> 33:48.693
[whimpering] Ma'am, please!

33:48.777 --> 33:51.196
- Salt. Salt. Salt.
- [dramatic quirky music continues]

33:55.867 --> 33:57.202
[Mi-rae sighs]

33:57.285 --> 33:58.578
All good?

33:58.662 --> 33:59.746
[cell phone buzzing]

33:59.829 --> 34:00.914
[Mi-ji] Yes.

34:00.997 --> 34:03.083
DAY TEN

34:03.208 --> 34:07.087
[music builds slowly]

34:07.170 --> 34:08.588
I told you not to come back!

34:08.672 --> 34:09.714
Wait, ma'am.

34:09.798 --> 34:11.758
[dramatic quirky music continues]

34:11.841 --> 34:12.884
[gasps]

34:14.636 --> 34:16.304
- [video game chime]
- [cell phone buzzing]

34:16.388 --> 34:19.224
[Mi-ji] I heard Childal
is trending these days.

34:19.307 --> 34:20.600
[sighs]

34:20.684 --> 34:21.643
[cash register dinging]

34:21.726 --> 34:23.853
[Mi-rae] Don't send me this crap.

34:23.937 --> 34:24.938
Shit.

34:26.022 --> 34:27.440
[groans]

34:28.024 --> 34:29.609
[breathes deeply]

34:29.693 --> 34:31.903
[music concludes]

34:32.862 --> 34:34.948
TWO WEEKS LATER

34:35.031 --> 34:37.617
[soft daring music playing]

34:52.007 --> 34:53.383
[grunting]

34:55.093 --> 34:56.136
[exhales]

35:08.440 --> 35:11.026
[Mi-ji] Please take a look
just once, ma'am.

35:11.109 --> 35:13.236
- Okay, fine.
- [gloomy quirky music playing]

35:13.862 --> 35:14.946
[Mi-ji] I'll go now.

35:15.572 --> 35:16.865
I'm leaving.

35:21.536 --> 35:26.397
TO BE DEMOLISHED

35:28.585 --> 35:30.253
- What do I do?
- [music concludes]

35:30.337 --> 35:32.839
That wraps up
the administrative sanction case.

35:33.923 --> 35:38.261
Oh, about that whistleblowing case
I was on as an external investigator,

35:38.345 --> 35:40.096
I heard it was closed.

35:40.180 --> 35:42.140
Can I ask what the outcome was?

35:42.223 --> 35:44.392
No special measures were taken.

35:44.476 --> 35:46.311
The employee withdrew the complaint.

35:46.978 --> 35:48.355
Did she say why?

35:48.438 --> 35:53.026
I'm not sure, but she withdrew it
as soon as the investigation began.

35:53.109 --> 35:54.110
[chuckles]

35:54.194 --> 35:56.655
Maybe she was afraid of
a false accusation charge.

35:59.616 --> 36:00.825
[whispers] Who's "she"?

36:00.909 --> 36:02.118
Yu Mi-rae, right?

36:02.202 --> 36:03.244
[scoffs]

36:07.123 --> 36:09.292
- [wind whistling]
- [birds chirping]

36:14.547 --> 36:15.757
Mi-yeong.

36:15.840 --> 36:19.386
Have you seen the chair
that was over there covered in tape?

36:19.469 --> 36:21.179
The broken one?

36:21.262 --> 36:22.514
Have you seen it?

36:22.597 --> 36:25.016
I took it out this morning with the trash.

36:25.100 --> 36:26.851
Weren't you going to throw it away?

36:27.435 --> 36:29.187
Why would you…

36:31.356 --> 36:32.607
[Se-jin exhales]

36:33.525 --> 36:35.694
Why did you do something
I didn't tell you to?

36:36.361 --> 36:38.488
Because you don't ask for anything.

36:38.571 --> 36:41.449
- You said to take initiative.
- I didn't mean cleaning, you know?

36:41.533 --> 36:42.826
You're dodging the issue.

36:43.368 --> 36:45.870
I hired a business partner, not a janitor.

36:45.954 --> 36:47.080
[sighs]

36:47.706 --> 36:51.584
A business partner
is someone who works with you.

36:51.668 --> 36:53.837
You really know your words.

36:53.920 --> 36:55.380
It's like talking to a dictionary.

36:55.463 --> 36:56.423
[]

36:57.048 --> 36:59.134
If it's about the chair,

36:59.217 --> 37:01.010
I'll buy a new one tomorrow.

37:03.638 --> 37:05.557
You were just insincere.

37:08.727 --> 37:10.145
When I had an office job,

37:11.771 --> 37:14.566
I saw people submitting
empty resumes like yours.

37:15.817 --> 37:18.611
And they were either
insincere or fearless.

37:19.487 --> 37:22.741
I was advised not to hire them,
but I always did.

37:23.408 --> 37:25.368
Because fearless people are rare.

37:26.703 --> 37:29.622
Then I'd watch them for a week
without assigning anything.

37:29.706 --> 37:32.375
You can see who's a hit and who's a miss.

37:33.668 --> 37:36.045
Fear of messing up
keeps some people from trying new things.

37:36.129 --> 37:38.298
They can't stick it out till the end.

37:38.381 --> 37:41.342
I hired you because
I thought you were fearless, Mi-yeong.

37:41.426 --> 37:42.927
But you're a miss.

37:46.306 --> 37:48.391
It's not "Mi-yeong." I'm Mi-ji.

37:50.101 --> 37:52.520
You don't even know my name.

37:53.188 --> 37:55.064
Why do you talk
like you know all about me?

37:55.857 --> 37:57.776
[melancholic music playing]

37:58.651 --> 38:00.612
Watching someone
without assigning them work

38:00.695 --> 38:02.614
isn't some brilliant strategy.

38:03.198 --> 38:04.532
That's just bullying.

38:05.200 --> 38:06.951
You say I can do whatever I want,

38:07.035 --> 38:10.121
but you just leave me hanging
and judge me however you like.

38:10.205 --> 38:11.748
It's like playing with a bug,

38:11.831 --> 38:14.375
pulling off its legs
just to see how long it lasts.

38:14.459 --> 38:16.753
You really find that fun?
Why are you so cruel?

38:16.836 --> 38:18.671
How could you treat someone like that?

38:18.755 --> 38:21.508
[breathes heavily]

38:22.801 --> 38:23.802
Pardon?

38:24.928 --> 38:26.012
[sighs]

38:29.516 --> 38:30.850
[Se-jin] I mean…

38:37.148 --> 38:38.399
[bag rustling]

38:39.025 --> 38:40.193
[Mi-rae sobbing]

38:40.276 --> 38:42.111
Oh! Oh! [screams]

38:42.195 --> 38:43.279
[bike crashes]

38:43.363 --> 38:45.490
- [music fades]
- What… What happened?

38:45.573 --> 38:47.700
What is it? What's wrong?

38:47.784 --> 38:50.495
- [Mi-rae groans]
- [Se-jin] What happened?

38:50.578 --> 38:52.038
- [groans]
- [running footsteps]

38:53.998 --> 38:55.041
[Mi-rae groans]

38:58.545 --> 39:00.421
Why are you lying there?

39:04.801 --> 39:06.886
[groans]

39:09.347 --> 39:10.348
[sighs]

39:13.393 --> 39:14.644
[groans]

39:15.436 --> 39:17.647
[breathes deeply]

39:19.148 --> 39:21.359
I should've stayed seated facing the wall.

39:21.442 --> 39:23.361
Why did I have to take the bait?

39:23.444 --> 39:24.988
[breathes deeply]

39:25.822 --> 39:28.116
Should I just come clean to Mi-rae?

39:29.868 --> 39:32.161
[groans] Get it together, you dummy.

39:32.245 --> 39:35.790
Stop trying to pass the buck
and clean up your mess.

39:35.874 --> 39:38.334
[breathes deeply]

39:43.590 --> 39:44.674
[groans]

39:45.592 --> 39:47.927
There's still salt on me.

39:54.517 --> 39:55.560
[sighs]

39:58.187 --> 39:59.272
Mi-rae?

40:02.025 --> 40:04.152
[soft music playing]

40:04.235 --> 40:07.488
[music turns romantic]

40:10.074 --> 40:12.660
[heartbeat thumping]

40:13.161 --> 40:15.413
[soft romantic music continues]

40:31.137 --> 40:34.140
[Mi-ji] Lee Ho-su? Why is he here?

40:34.724 --> 40:35.725
What?

40:36.601 --> 40:39.187
What do you mean…
I mean, what about you?

40:40.104 --> 40:41.314
- What about me?
- [music fades]

40:41.397 --> 40:45.068
Why aren't you answering my calls
after disappearing and making me worry?

40:45.151 --> 40:46.778
- Did you block me?
- [sighs]

40:46.861 --> 40:48.529
[automated voice]
The person you're calling…

40:48.613 --> 40:50.073
No, I didn't…

40:50.198 --> 40:52.700
- [automated voice] Please try again later.
- So what?

40:52.784 --> 40:54.827
Do I have to answer every time you call?

40:55.954 --> 40:56.955
Gosh.

40:58.957 --> 41:00.041
What happened…

41:00.959 --> 41:02.126
with the whistleblowing case?

41:03.461 --> 41:06.214
How do you know about that?
Are you checking up on me?

41:06.297 --> 41:07.632
You don't remember seeing me?

41:11.052 --> 41:13.012
As an external investigator?

41:14.764 --> 41:16.391
Look, what's your point?

41:17.684 --> 41:20.436
If you have something to say, text me.
I have to go.

41:24.232 --> 41:26.025
Your office is that way.

41:27.068 --> 41:28.611
[mutters] Darn it.

41:35.410 --> 41:36.744
Can we talk?

41:36.828 --> 41:38.913
I'd rather not put this in writing.

41:38.997 --> 41:40.206
Then talk.

41:40.289 --> 41:42.125
We can't discuss this near the office…

41:42.208 --> 41:43.543
Hey, Yu Mi-rae!

41:44.502 --> 41:46.879
What's running away going to solve?

41:46.963 --> 41:49.507
This is about you.
Let's at least talk about it.

41:50.425 --> 41:51.884
Come on. Make time.

41:52.635 --> 41:54.846
Anything more
would be a hassle, even for me.

41:57.181 --> 41:58.766
Fine, let's meet this weekend.

41:58.850 --> 41:59.976
Saturday night?

42:01.019 --> 42:02.603
We can decide where later.

42:10.695 --> 42:12.780
[Mi-rae] What? Ho-su?

42:16.617 --> 42:17.660
[sighs]

42:19.203 --> 42:22.081
Don't tell me you made plans with him.

42:22.165 --> 42:24.792
He just wants to talk for a bit.

42:24.876 --> 42:26.961
It'd be weird to flat-out refuse.

42:27.503 --> 42:29.255
But did you run into him?

42:29.338 --> 42:32.633
He said something about
being an external investigator earlier.

42:32.717 --> 42:33.968
Don't meet him.

42:34.052 --> 42:35.928
What if he figures it out?

42:36.596 --> 42:39.807
He won't. He still thinks I'm you.

42:39.891 --> 42:42.018
Don't you remember back in high school?

42:42.101 --> 42:43.269
[Mi-ji] Who is it?

42:46.773 --> 42:49.317
[Mi-rae] He knew exactly who was who
even with towels on our heads.

42:49.400 --> 42:50.568
TO MI-JI

42:54.739 --> 42:55.740
[Ho-su] Who are you?

42:58.576 --> 42:59.702
Are you really Mi-ji?

43:01.079 --> 43:02.205
[sighs]

43:02.288 --> 43:03.664
He can't tell.

43:04.332 --> 43:06.876
Even if he suspects,
we know how to shut him up.

43:06.959 --> 43:09.587
What was it… absorbed-self…

43:09.670 --> 43:11.798
- Self-absorbed.
- Right.

43:11.881 --> 43:14.300
[Mi-rae] Just listen to me.
Don't meet him.

43:14.383 --> 43:17.095
We promised
not to interfere in each other's lives.

43:17.178 --> 43:18.805
[inhales]

43:19.388 --> 43:20.807
But you know…

43:21.766 --> 43:24.727
some things could happen

43:24.811 --> 43:28.022
that force us to get involved
in each other's lives.

43:28.106 --> 43:30.441
Like an accident or a disaster.

43:30.525 --> 43:31.818
Did you do something?

43:31.901 --> 43:33.236
[innocently] No!

43:33.319 --> 43:36.405
I didn't do anything, I swear.
Honestly, I just…

43:36.989 --> 43:39.992
want to do something. Anything.

43:40.076 --> 43:41.077
Look, don't meet him.

43:41.911 --> 43:43.788
I don't want you to see him as me.

43:43.871 --> 43:45.206
Okay?

43:46.207 --> 43:48.584
- Answer me.
- Okay.

43:49.627 --> 43:51.879
I said okay. I'm hanging up.

43:52.505 --> 43:54.048
[cell phone beeping, thudding]

43:54.590 --> 43:56.259
Jeez, what do I do?

43:57.218 --> 43:59.679
Seeing Ho-su is enough to freak her out.

43:59.762 --> 44:01.639
If she finds out what I did…

44:01.722 --> 44:04.058
Oh, man!

44:04.142 --> 44:05.393
What do I do?

44:05.476 --> 44:06.644
[cell phone buzzes]

44:11.149 --> 44:12.942
[Ho-su] Saturday at Gwanghwamun?

44:14.443 --> 44:16.070
[Mi-ji] Sorry, but…

44:16.154 --> 44:17.196
[soft music playing]

44:17.280 --> 44:21.367
I ran into Mi-rae recently.

44:21.450 --> 44:24.370
And it seemed like
she was having a hard time.

44:24.453 --> 44:26.497
What's running away going to solve?

44:27.081 --> 44:29.500
This is a big problem.
Let's at least talk about it.

44:33.921 --> 44:36.841
- [music concludes]
- Does she still have me blocked?

44:37.758 --> 44:39.802
Unbelievable…

44:40.803 --> 44:42.513
[tender music playing]

44:42.597 --> 44:43.472
[Ho-su] Mi-rae.

44:44.098 --> 44:46.726
[heartbeat thumping]

44:56.152 --> 44:57.737
- Gosh!
- [music concludes]

44:57.820 --> 45:00.239
- [traffic rumbling]
- [sirens wailing in distance]

45:00.740 --> 45:03.242
[quirky music playing]

45:09.999 --> 45:12.251
No, this isn't right.

45:12.335 --> 45:13.669
[cell phone buzzes]

45:15.421 --> 45:16.839
[music fades]

45:17.632 --> 45:19.967
[Mi-ji] Who meets up
near the office on a weekend?

45:22.929 --> 45:23.971
[phone buzzes]

45:24.055 --> 45:25.056
Oh!

45:27.558 --> 45:29.352
[Ho-su] Then where?

45:29.435 --> 45:30.436
[tender music playing]

45:30.519 --> 45:31.520
Where?

45:32.313 --> 45:35.524
There are a million places to go.

45:35.608 --> 45:37.693
Namsan? Absolutely.

45:37.777 --> 45:39.320
Hongdae? Definitely.

45:40.488 --> 45:43.991
Hit Gwanghwamun,
then loop Samcheong-dong and Insa-dong.

45:44.075 --> 45:47.578
And at night, you have to see
the Rainbow Fountain at the Hangang River.

45:52.375 --> 45:54.043
Hey, Seoul mouse.

45:54.126 --> 45:56.003
Recommend something local.

45:56.879 --> 45:58.631
What's your favorite spot in Seoul?

46:00.174 --> 46:03.594
I feel like
there's nothing to see in Seoul.

46:07.098 --> 46:09.558
[scoffs] Nothing? Come on.

46:09.642 --> 46:11.227
This whole book is about Seoul.

46:13.646 --> 46:14.730
Here.

46:15.481 --> 46:17.441
Check off everywhere you haven't been.

46:18.401 --> 46:19.318
Why?

46:19.402 --> 46:21.570
We'll see each other in Seoul anyway.

46:22.196 --> 46:24.782
It's more fun if we meet somewhere
neither of us has been.

46:24.865 --> 46:27.034
It'll be like stepping on fresh snow.

46:37.336 --> 46:39.338
Why aren't you going home?

46:39.422 --> 46:40.715
No one's home.

46:41.215 --> 46:42.591
Everyone's in Seoul.

46:42.675 --> 46:43.718
Then…

46:44.552 --> 46:46.679
you should've gone with them
instead of reading this.

46:46.762 --> 46:47.847
Mm.

46:49.473 --> 46:50.641
Later.

46:51.684 --> 46:53.311
I'll go later.

46:55.438 --> 46:58.190
For my family,
Seoul is just where Mi-rae's hospital is.

47:03.571 --> 47:06.324
Also, I'm waiting for you right now.

47:06.907 --> 47:09.035
You've been going over
the wrong answers for hours.

47:09.118 --> 47:10.411
Wrap it up already!

47:17.835 --> 47:19.712
[music concludes]

47:19.795 --> 47:21.255
[pop music thumping over speakers]

47:21.339 --> 47:24.216
[host] Welcome!
We only have bar seats left. Is that okay?

47:24.717 --> 47:26.052
Uh, yes!

47:26.135 --> 47:27.386
This way, please.

47:27.887 --> 47:30.598
[loud lively chatter]

47:34.810 --> 47:36.854
[high-pitched ringing]

47:37.521 --> 47:39.690
[muffled] Gosh, we barely made it in.

47:41.150 --> 47:44.779
[loudly] I guess all the restaurants
are booked on weekends.

47:45.821 --> 47:48.074
Yeah, I haven't eaten yet either.

47:48.699 --> 47:50.201
What?

47:50.284 --> 47:51.619
Here are your menus.

47:58.376 --> 48:00.419
They have set menus for…

48:01.712 --> 48:04.048
- [loud chatter]
- [pop music continues thumping]

48:07.093 --> 48:08.302
[sighs]

48:14.934 --> 48:15.935
What?

48:22.608 --> 48:24.860
Did I do something wrong? What's up?

48:26.320 --> 48:27.947
You said you had something to say.

48:28.030 --> 48:30.991
This doesn't feel like the right place
for a serious talk.

48:32.159 --> 48:35.037
Are you trying to be
considerate right now?

48:39.792 --> 48:42.169
You're not the only one who hates noise.

48:42.253 --> 48:44.588
You really are self-absorbed.

48:44.672 --> 48:45.798
[scoffs]

48:45.881 --> 48:47.508
I was just asking.

48:48.634 --> 48:50.052
Where do we go, then?

48:50.136 --> 48:52.304
Every restaurant around here is packed.

48:56.892 --> 48:59.478
You don't mind walking
for ten minutes, do you?

49:03.941 --> 49:06.485
Wow! [giggles]

49:07.445 --> 49:08.571
Oh my God.

49:10.656 --> 49:11.824
Gosh.

49:12.575 --> 49:15.828
[gasps] It's beautiful.

49:15.911 --> 49:18.038
[sentimental music playing]

49:28.424 --> 49:30.801
Okay, selfie time.

49:35.431 --> 49:36.640
What?

49:36.724 --> 49:39.810
Is this your first time
seeing the Hangang River or something?

49:41.854 --> 49:43.147
Are you kidding?

49:43.230 --> 49:45.441
I'm a Seoulite. How can this be my first?

49:46.108 --> 49:49.028
Then why are you so obsessed with it
if you see it all the time?

49:50.613 --> 49:53.782
It's not the same
as seeing it from the subway.

50:03.250 --> 50:04.543
Now that you mention it…

50:05.544 --> 50:07.421
it has been ages since I've been here.

50:07.505 --> 50:11.634
See? Stop working all the time
and enjoy things like this sometimes.

50:13.427 --> 50:14.470
So…

50:15.262 --> 50:17.223
what are we supposed to eat here?

50:17.306 --> 50:19.391
Isn't it obvious? It's the Hangang River.

50:20.226 --> 50:21.936
[Mi-ji] By the Hangang River…

50:22.019 --> 50:23.854
[tender music playing]

50:23.938 --> 50:25.356
…you eat ramyun.

50:25.439 --> 50:26.649
Not cup ramyun though.

50:26.732 --> 50:29.735
It has to be the one
made with the ramyun cooker.

50:30.945 --> 50:32.696
Isn't it all just the same?

50:33.906 --> 50:37.117
Are you kidding?
You use packaged ramyun with the cooker.

50:37.201 --> 50:40.120
The noodles are different.
And no cook-in-the-bag method.

50:40.204 --> 50:42.623
You've got to use the cooker.
It's the whole vibe.

50:43.624 --> 50:45.251
Everything's a whole vibe to you.

50:45.334 --> 50:46.669
[Mi-ji inhales]

50:46.752 --> 50:49.505
Jeez. You'll get it once you taste it.

50:49.588 --> 50:52.341
[music]

50:59.765 --> 51:02.685
[music concludes]

51:14.280 --> 51:16.740
How is it? It's different, right?

51:18.659 --> 51:20.119
I told you.

51:21.245 --> 51:22.413
You're right.

51:22.997 --> 51:24.164
[exhales]

51:24.248 --> 51:27.084
No wonder Mi-ji kept raving
about Hangang River ramyun.

51:31.755 --> 51:34.008
So, what did you want to talk about?

51:35.843 --> 51:38.387
Eat first. We'll talk after.

51:39.513 --> 51:42.057
Why are you dragging it out? Just say it.

51:53.360 --> 51:55.070
Did you drop the case…

51:57.364 --> 51:58.574
because of me?

52:01.243 --> 52:03.329
What do you mean "because of you"?

52:04.246 --> 52:05.331
[sighs]

52:07.124 --> 52:08.334
That day…

52:11.295 --> 52:12.630
I didn't expect to run into you.

52:12.713 --> 52:14.006
INTERNAL REPORT INVESTIGATION

52:14.840 --> 52:18.177
You know how it works at your company…

52:18.260 --> 52:21.680
When someone blows the whistle,
our firm steps in to investigate.

52:21.764 --> 52:22.931
[knocking on door]

52:23.015 --> 52:24.600
[Ho-su] It just so happened

52:24.683 --> 52:27.895
that I was sent in to cover
for my supervising attorney that day.

52:28.479 --> 52:29.813
Sorry I'm late.

52:32.524 --> 52:34.985
[Mi-ji] So what exactly was
"because of you"?

52:35.653 --> 52:37.404
In cases like this,

52:38.197 --> 52:39.907
when it's about sexual misconduct,

52:40.741 --> 52:42.868
sometimes the victim drops the case

52:42.951 --> 52:45.287
because they're worried
about rumors spreading.

52:45.788 --> 52:48.582
I don't know any of the details,
so don't worry.

52:48.666 --> 52:51.210
Once I knew it was you,
I didn't even look at the files.

52:51.335 --> 52:53.379
[pensive music playing]

52:53.462 --> 52:57.132
Are we talking about Director Choi?

52:58.884 --> 53:00.135
Director Choi?

53:00.761 --> 53:02.930
I thought it was
Lead Specialist Park Sang-yeong.

53:05.057 --> 53:07.643
I just feel bad for Mr. Park.

53:07.726 --> 53:09.728
He shouldn't have looked out for her.

53:09.812 --> 53:13.357
[Mi-ji] Mi-rae.
Did something else happen?

53:16.985 --> 53:20.698
If you dropped the case because of me…

53:22.616 --> 53:24.243
then let’s figure something out.

53:26.036 --> 53:29.581
The internal process may be over,
but you might have a strong case in court.

53:29.665 --> 53:32.376
We promised
not to interfere in each other's lives.

53:32.459 --> 53:33.335
[sighs]

53:33.419 --> 53:35.879
- I know lawyers who specialize in this…
- Ho-su.

53:35.963 --> 53:37.256
You haven't changed at all.

53:38.382 --> 53:39.299
[music concludes]

53:39.383 --> 53:42.302
- What?
- The world doesn't revolve around you.

53:42.928 --> 53:46.306
Why would I drop it because of you?
I decided for my own reasons.

53:46.390 --> 53:49.852
I mean, you avoided me
as soon as you saw me that day.

53:49.935 --> 53:52.104
That's exactly what I mean
by self-absorbed.

53:52.187 --> 53:53.605
Why would I avoid you?

53:54.773 --> 53:58.068
I'm swamped with this new project
and don't have time for anything else.

53:58.152 --> 54:00.696
That's why I dropped it.
Don't flatter yourself.

54:04.867 --> 54:05.993
So was it…

54:07.077 --> 54:08.328
really all in my head?

54:08.412 --> 54:09.872
Of course it was.

54:10.622 --> 54:13.125
Your supervising attorney
doesn't know our history.

54:13.208 --> 54:15.085
He just sent you to cover him, right?

54:16.128 --> 54:18.922
What? Are you concerned
because she was a classmate?

54:20.340 --> 54:22.342
It was just a crazy coincidence.

54:23.177 --> 54:24.178
Wasn't it?

54:26.096 --> 54:27.347
You're right.

54:28.891 --> 54:31.059
I don't think he sent me on purpose.

54:31.852 --> 54:33.771
You made all that fuss over this?

54:34.396 --> 54:35.773
Gosh.

54:35.856 --> 54:38.650
How are you even a lawyer
when you're this soft?

54:40.068 --> 54:42.446
You probably work for free
half the time, don't you?

54:42.529 --> 54:44.072
You clearly don't know me.

54:44.656 --> 54:45.699
I've changed.

54:45.783 --> 54:48.327
And yet you're here with me on a weekend?

54:50.370 --> 54:51.747
You're still the same.

54:52.623 --> 54:55.918
Once something gets stuck in your mind,
you can never let it go.

54:56.585 --> 55:00.631
You get all fidgety,
like a kid with a pebble in his shoe.

55:04.426 --> 55:05.594
I do?

55:06.220 --> 55:07.971
Yes, you. Who else?

55:08.931 --> 55:10.891
Whatever. Just eat.

55:14.520 --> 55:15.687
[gentle pop song playing]

55:15.771 --> 55:17.606
[teacher] Why are you two still here?

55:18.398 --> 55:20.859
I'm waiting for Ho-su
to finish his review.

55:20.943 --> 55:23.153
What? He got a perfect score.

55:23.237 --> 55:24.655
Go home already!

55:24.738 --> 55:25.948
[door opens]

55:26.031 --> 55:28.033
[gentle pop song continues]

55:33.747 --> 55:35.249
What's up with you?

55:36.166 --> 55:38.627
- [book rustling]
- [singing in Korean]

55:38.710 --> 55:40.587
You didn't get anything wrong.

55:43.423 --> 55:45.717
There were a few…

55:46.718 --> 55:48.262
I just guessed on.

55:50.430 --> 55:56.353
[singing in Korean]

55:57.646 --> 56:03.527
[singing in Korean continues]

56:07.656 --> 56:11.159
[singing in Korean continues]

56:12.369 --> 56:15.789
[Mi-ji] Whether the pebble in his shoe
was the question he guessed on

56:16.373 --> 56:17.583
or me,

56:18.500 --> 56:20.002
I still don't know.

56:23.213 --> 56:24.882
Are you done? Let's get going.

56:24.965 --> 56:26.842
Aren't you heading back to work?

56:26.925 --> 56:28.802
The fountain's about to go off.

56:31.221 --> 56:34.933
What are you, a kid?
What's so great about a fountain?

56:35.017 --> 56:36.393
I thought you wanted to see it.

56:36.476 --> 56:39.313
- [music concludes]
- [scoffs] That must've been Mi-ji.

56:39.396 --> 56:41.815
You said it too. Don't you remember?

56:42.524 --> 56:45.736
When we came to Seoul for that mock exam.

56:49.865 --> 56:51.617
You remember the weirdest things.

56:52.951 --> 56:54.369
Hey, throw this away.

56:55.996 --> 56:57.039
Okay.

56:58.999 --> 57:00.083
I'll take it.

57:09.843 --> 57:10.886
[Mi-rae sighs]

57:13.805 --> 57:15.766
Why are you here at this hour?

57:15.849 --> 57:18.101
Do I need a reason to visit?

57:18.810 --> 57:21.521
[quirky music playing]

57:25.692 --> 57:27.486
It works just fine.

57:34.701 --> 57:37.079
[sighs] Why'd you do that?

57:38.372 --> 57:39.456
Do what?

57:40.999 --> 57:44.378
You really thought I wouldn't notice
if you didn't say anything?

57:46.588 --> 57:47.714
Pardon?

57:47.798 --> 57:49.967
[sighs] Jeez.

57:50.968 --> 57:53.011
You were riding drunk, weren’t you?

57:53.095 --> 57:55.514
Drunk biking is serious!

57:55.597 --> 57:58.141
[whispers]
If your mom finds out, you're dead.

57:58.225 --> 58:02.396
Come on, I wasn't drunk.

58:02.479 --> 58:05.482
Are you saying you were sober
when you fell off your bike?

58:05.565 --> 58:09.861
Does that make any sense?
You can ride without your hands or feet!

58:09.945 --> 58:11.989
Earlier, you were wobbling around

58:12.614 --> 58:14.282
like you were wasted.

58:14.366 --> 58:16.576
- It wasn’t drunk biking.
- Yes, it was.

58:24.376 --> 58:26.003
- [music fades]
- [Mi-rae clears throat]

58:26.086 --> 58:27.212
What the heck?

58:30.465 --> 58:34.386
[sighs] You seem off.
Even your hair's different.

58:34.469 --> 58:36.722
What's going on? Just talk to me.

58:37.597 --> 58:39.766
Even the old folks
in the neighborhood are worried,

58:39.850 --> 58:41.977
asking what's going on with Yu Candy.

58:42.060 --> 58:43.311
"Yu Can…"

58:44.396 --> 58:45.939
[in English] "You can do it?"

58:48.942 --> 58:52.112
[in Korean] Candy. The one from the anime.
She's sad, but strong.

58:52.195 --> 58:53.321
I see.

58:54.865 --> 58:57.075
Why is everyone so worried? I'm fine.

58:57.159 --> 58:59.202
The Youth Association President noticed.

58:59.286 --> 59:02.581
He said you looked miserable yesterday,
just moping around.

59:02.664 --> 59:06.293
How could I smile when I busted my knee
and there was blood everywhere?

59:06.376 --> 59:07.794
But that's what you do.

59:08.378 --> 59:10.630
Even when you got
your wisdom tooth pulled out,

59:10.714 --> 59:12.382
you were grinning like the Joker.

59:13.717 --> 59:16.094
How can anyone be cheerful 24/7?

59:16.678 --> 59:17.721
Exactly.

59:19.473 --> 59:20.724
[tender music playing]

59:20.807 --> 59:22.559
[Gyeong-gu] That's my point.

59:22.642 --> 59:26.521
You're always abnormally cheerful.

59:26.605 --> 59:28.440
That's why you're Yu Candy.

59:33.612 --> 59:35.030
[sighs]

59:36.740 --> 59:39.242
I haven't seen you so drained
since graduation.

59:40.619 --> 59:41.703
Mm.

59:42.996 --> 59:44.164
Really?

59:44.247 --> 59:45.332
Yeah.

59:47.125 --> 59:48.293
See you.

59:52.464 --> 59:53.799
[gate opens]

59:54.758 --> 59:55.926
[sighs]

59:56.009 --> 59:57.302
[gate closes]

59:58.303 --> 01:00:00.138
[door lock beeps]

01:00:01.306 --> 01:00:03.892
Hey, I just got home.

01:00:03.975 --> 01:00:05.143
[door lock beeps]

01:00:05.227 --> 01:00:07.854
[Mi-rae over phone] It's the weekend.
What took you so long?

01:00:07.938 --> 01:00:10.357
I went to see the Hangang River by myself.

01:00:11.733 --> 01:00:13.777
Hey, by any chance…

01:00:13.860 --> 01:00:15.070
[chair scraping]

01:00:15.153 --> 01:00:19.908
…do you have anything
you want to say to me?

01:00:21.451 --> 01:00:22.786
What do you mean?

01:00:25.914 --> 01:00:26.998
Just…

01:00:30.585 --> 01:00:34.131
Have you ever wanted to see
the Rainbow Fountain?

01:00:36.633 --> 01:00:38.093
The Rainbow Fountain?

01:00:40.053 --> 01:00:41.680
I think so, maybe.

01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:44.891
You used to talk about it all the time.

01:00:45.600 --> 01:00:46.601
Why?

01:00:47.269 --> 01:00:50.355
No reason. I don't think
we ever talked about it before.

01:00:51.773 --> 01:00:53.150
Anyway.

01:00:54.151 --> 01:00:55.402
Okay.

01:00:56.319 --> 01:00:59.781
Do you know your door's broken?

01:00:59.865 --> 01:01:02.492
Right. It doesn't close, does it?

01:01:02.576 --> 01:01:05.370
If it bothers you,
just change the doorknob.

01:01:05.453 --> 01:01:07.372
[gentle music playing]

01:01:07.455 --> 01:01:08.707
Are you…

01:01:09.708 --> 01:01:11.126
still having a hard time?

01:01:12.294 --> 01:01:13.336
What?

01:01:14.004 --> 01:01:16.339
I mean, I always left my door open anyway.

01:01:17.757 --> 01:01:19.634
You know that's not what I meant.

01:01:22.721 --> 01:01:26.766
[exhales] Come on. I'm Yu Candy.

01:01:26.850 --> 01:01:28.977
Why would I be having a hard time?

01:01:29.060 --> 01:01:31.980
Gosh, who's worrying about who here?

01:01:32.898 --> 01:01:35.692
Mi-rae, worry about yourself.

01:01:38.278 --> 01:01:41.823
- Mi-ji, you--
- [Mi-ji] Oh, right.

01:01:41.907 --> 01:01:44.576
Your heels are too high.

01:01:44.659 --> 01:01:48.705
My feet got blisters on the back,
and they bled. It was a mess.

01:01:48.788 --> 01:01:50.123
Don't yours ever hurt?

01:01:51.208 --> 01:01:54.461
I've worn them enough
that I've got calluses now.

01:01:55.462 --> 01:01:57.589
Why? Did they hurt that much?

01:01:58.632 --> 01:02:01.635
No, I'll get used to it soon enough.

01:02:01.718 --> 01:02:03.553
We've got the same feet, after all.

01:02:05.764 --> 01:02:08.808
I suppose. We are the same.

01:02:13.313 --> 01:02:14.439
Okay.

01:02:14.522 --> 01:02:17.859
Anyway, get some sleep. I'll call soon.

01:02:18.360 --> 01:02:20.111
- [Mi-rae] Okay.
- [Mi-ji] All right.

01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:21.780
[cell phone beeps]

01:02:25.200 --> 01:02:26.993
CALL ENDED
MI-JI

01:02:29.037 --> 01:02:30.789
[Mi-ji] We're more alike than anyone…

01:02:30.872 --> 01:02:31.957
CALL ENDED
MI-RAE

01:02:32.040 --> 01:02:35.627
…so why did I always think
you were my opposite?

01:02:36.962 --> 01:02:39.506
I'm not sure who I was trying to be.

01:02:41.675 --> 01:02:42.717
Why…

01:02:43.969 --> 01:02:45.929
did I think I knew you?

01:02:49.891 --> 01:02:52.560
[music fades]

01:03:04.572 --> 01:03:05.949
What are you doing?

01:03:07.117 --> 01:03:09.202
Just breathing. Why?

01:03:10.620 --> 01:03:11.913
[scoffs]

01:03:11.997 --> 01:03:14.124
I heard you don't work
on the farm anymore.

01:03:14.833 --> 01:03:17.210
I'm going to the bank,
so take care of Grandma today.

01:03:17.294 --> 01:03:18.795
Wash up and go to the hospital.

01:03:18.878 --> 01:03:20.338
Wait, Mom…

01:03:23.550 --> 01:03:24.634
[sighs]

01:03:28.972 --> 01:03:30.515
[nurse] Mi-ji, you're here.

01:03:31.683 --> 01:03:33.810
You didn't come last week. Were you sick?

01:03:34.394 --> 01:03:36.563
- No, I was busy with work.
- [nurse] I see.

01:03:37.147 --> 01:03:40.692
Grandma, sit up and look who's here.

01:03:44.946 --> 01:03:48.033
You always tell her not to come,
but you miss her when she's not here.

01:03:48.116 --> 01:03:49.576
Who's that over there?

01:03:49.659 --> 01:03:54.706
FALL RISK
BED REST ONLY

01:04:00.920 --> 01:04:02.088
Mi-ji.

01:04:03.506 --> 01:04:04.549
[nurse] That's right.

01:04:04.632 --> 01:04:07.093
Now that Mi-ji's here,
let's get you dolled up.

01:04:07.886 --> 01:04:09.971
I'll get some water to wash you up.

01:04:10.597 --> 01:04:11.598
Let me.

01:04:11.681 --> 01:04:13.350
- I'll do it.
- No, it's okay.

01:04:13.433 --> 01:04:14.601
I got it.

01:04:15.393 --> 01:04:17.520
[footsteps departing]

01:04:18.021 --> 01:04:20.148
[Ho-su] Here's the draft
for Chairman Choi's settlement.

01:04:20.231 --> 01:04:21.608
I wrote it up, but…

01:04:22.192 --> 01:04:24.319
I'm worried it might be a bit much.

01:04:24.402 --> 01:04:26.571
Right, it's probably best to revise it.

01:04:27.280 --> 01:04:28.782
Go for no compensation.

01:04:30.241 --> 01:04:31.284
Pardon?

01:04:31.368 --> 01:04:34.537
[Chung-gu] Once the suspended license
was mentioned, the victim gave in.

01:04:34.621 --> 01:04:37.999
All that's left is a signature.

01:04:38.083 --> 01:04:40.585
Thanks to you, it all worked out.

01:04:41.503 --> 01:04:46.049
But there was real damage done.
There should be some compensation…

01:04:46.132 --> 01:04:48.718
You're overthinking it again.

01:04:49.260 --> 01:04:51.388
Our client is Chairman Choi, remember?

01:04:51.471 --> 01:04:53.306
You did great, so why the long face?

01:04:54.557 --> 01:04:55.558
Let's go.

01:04:55.642 --> 01:04:59.145
That cheapskate Chairman Choi
is treating us to something fancy tonight.

01:04:59.229 --> 01:05:00.397
I'm good, actually.

01:05:00.480 --> 01:05:02.148
[Chung-gu] He likes you.

01:05:02.232 --> 01:05:06.194
The guy may be a pain,
but getting to know him won't hurt you.

01:05:07.153 --> 01:05:09.030
Might as well make a good impression.

01:05:11.408 --> 01:05:12.867
[sighs softly]

01:05:22.419 --> 01:05:24.504
- Mr. Lee.
- Yes?

01:05:26.840 --> 01:05:30.969
How did you know the whistleblower
was my classmate?

01:05:31.678 --> 01:05:33.179
I read the case file.

01:05:33.263 --> 01:05:35.849
Your high school has a unique name.
Duson High.

01:05:38.393 --> 01:05:40.437
Did you send me on purpose

01:05:41.521 --> 01:05:43.440
because she was my classmate?

01:05:44.524 --> 01:05:45.817
Of course I did.

01:05:46.651 --> 01:05:48.736
- Really?
- [Chung-hu] Yes.

01:05:48.820 --> 01:05:51.156
- To get her to drop the case.
- [pensive music playing]

01:05:51.239 --> 01:05:53.450
It's best to wrap things up quickly.

01:05:55.243 --> 01:05:57.203
If you're asking for the deeper reason,

01:05:57.287 --> 01:06:00.457
our client is the company,
not the employee.

01:06:01.791 --> 01:06:05.462
They just got a new CEO,
so they're sensitive about the media.

01:06:08.840 --> 01:06:11.885
[grunting]

01:06:15.805 --> 01:06:17.265
Don't take it too personally.

01:06:18.308 --> 01:06:20.435
It's like Chairman Choi's case.

01:06:20.518 --> 01:06:23.938
Sure, the victim feels wronged,
and the perpetrator's in the wrong.

01:06:24.022 --> 01:06:25.648
But winning comes first.

01:06:28.401 --> 01:06:29.611
That's our job.

01:06:35.909 --> 01:06:39.454
[Mi-ji] Once something gets stuck
in your mind, you can never let it go.

01:06:39.537 --> 01:06:42.749
You get all fidgety,
like a kid with a pebble in his shoe.

01:06:44.375 --> 01:06:45.460
[Chung-hu] You ready?

01:06:45.543 --> 01:06:47.837
Chairman Choi has sent a car.

01:06:48.505 --> 01:06:49.506
I'm…

01:06:52.509 --> 01:06:53.760
not going.

01:06:54.552 --> 01:06:55.637
What?

01:07:00.725 --> 01:07:01.726
Are you serious?

01:07:05.188 --> 01:07:06.272
Yes.

01:07:09.484 --> 01:07:10.902
Okay.

01:07:10.985 --> 01:07:12.946
Good work today. Go get some rest.

01:07:39.347 --> 01:07:42.725
[music concludes]

01:07:46.145 --> 01:07:48.565
You're not sick or anything, are you?

01:07:49.148 --> 01:07:50.483
[sighs]

01:07:50.567 --> 01:07:53.152
Have you ever seen me get sick?

01:07:53.903 --> 01:07:56.155
I'm always fit as a fiddle.

01:07:59.409 --> 01:08:03.079
Was it tough for you in Seoul?

01:08:03.830 --> 01:08:07.208
Why would it be?
I just took some food to Mi-rae.

01:08:10.628 --> 01:08:12.171
Mi-rae.

01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:16.634
[gentle music box playing]

01:08:21.556 --> 01:08:23.182
You knew?

01:08:23.683 --> 01:08:26.144
Even though I'm counting my days,

01:08:26.894 --> 01:08:30.273
I'll still recognize you, Mi-rae.

01:08:36.904 --> 01:08:39.324
Aren't you going to ask why I'm here?

01:08:39.407 --> 01:08:41.117
What's the point?

01:08:41.868 --> 01:08:45.747
I bet you kept it all in, barely hung on,

01:08:45.830 --> 01:08:50.293
until you couldn't anymore.

01:08:53.838 --> 01:08:54.964
No.

01:08:56.966 --> 01:08:59.010
I couldn't hang on. [sniffles]

01:09:00.928 --> 01:09:03.723
I ran away, Grandma. [sobs]

01:09:05.266 --> 01:09:06.851
Good for you.

01:09:06.934 --> 01:09:08.770
You did well, Mi-rae.

01:09:09.395 --> 01:09:11.731
You did the right thing.

01:09:15.109 --> 01:09:18.613
- Grandma.
- You did well.

01:09:19.739 --> 01:09:22.909
[Gyeong-min shouting]
You still haven't delivered the documents?

01:09:25.745 --> 01:09:27.705
Do you go there to hang out?

01:09:27.789 --> 01:09:29.499
The landlord can be quite difficult…

01:09:29.582 --> 01:09:31.000
Didn't you know that beforehand?

01:09:31.084 --> 01:09:34.128
You were the one who volunteered
and took the job.

01:09:34.212 --> 01:09:36.923
Then you should've followed through,
Ms. Yu Mi-rae.

01:09:37.006 --> 01:09:38.257
I won't say more.

01:09:38.925 --> 01:09:41.135
You'll be taking
full responsibility anyway.

01:09:42.095 --> 01:09:43.096
Go.

01:09:46.474 --> 01:09:47.975
Take this with you!

01:10:01.239 --> 01:10:02.407
[mouths] Shit.

01:10:06.619 --> 01:10:07.495
[door bell chimes]

01:10:13.960 --> 01:10:16.504
[chuckles] Hello, ma'am.

01:10:19.090 --> 01:10:20.508
Ma'am.

01:10:20.591 --> 01:10:24.637
Could you hear me out just for a second
before you throw salt at me?

01:10:25.263 --> 01:10:26.264
Seriously.

01:10:27.140 --> 01:10:29.767
Ma'am, then I will…

01:10:29.851 --> 01:10:31.978
leave the documents here.

01:10:32.061 --> 01:10:33.730
Just read the proposal, please…

01:10:33.813 --> 01:10:34.939
Ma'am!

01:10:36.107 --> 01:10:37.567
Jeez.

01:10:37.650 --> 01:10:39.736
What did I ever do to deserve this?

01:10:39.819 --> 01:10:41.904
Am I not a person? Did I break the law?

01:10:41.988 --> 01:10:43.239
I'm just doing my job.

01:10:43.322 --> 01:10:45.241
Just like you chop green onions
and clean giblets,

01:10:45.324 --> 01:10:47.160
I'm just doing my job too.

01:10:47.243 --> 01:10:50.538
We're both trying to make a living here.
You don't have to treat me like this.

01:10:50.621 --> 01:10:52.457
I'm not asking you to sell
or sign anything.

01:10:52.540 --> 01:10:55.543
I just want you to read these documents.

01:10:55.626 --> 01:10:58.921
That's not such a terrible thing
for you to ruin my livelihood over!

01:10:59.005 --> 01:11:01.007
[pants]

01:11:04.177 --> 01:11:05.178
Are you done?

01:11:09.849 --> 01:11:10.850
Yes.

01:11:33.164 --> 01:11:34.540
[Mi-ji] What is this feeling?

01:11:34.624 --> 01:11:35.875
[soft daring music playing]

01:11:35.958 --> 01:11:37.919
[Mi-ji] I clearly messed everything up.

01:11:39.921 --> 01:11:41.756
But somehow, it's easier to breathe.

01:11:42.548 --> 01:11:44.217
For the first time in forever,

01:11:45.468 --> 01:11:48.554
I feel like I've taken off
an invisible mask.

01:12:01.192 --> 01:12:02.193
What?

01:12:02.276 --> 01:12:04.445
[gentle music continues]

01:12:12.078 --> 01:12:14.997
[music fades]

01:12:16.207 --> 01:12:17.375
[Ho-su] You're here.

01:12:23.923 --> 01:12:26.050
What is it? Do you have more to say?

01:12:30.012 --> 01:12:31.389
I want to say sorry.

01:12:32.139 --> 01:12:33.432
Sorry?

01:12:35.101 --> 01:12:39.647
That time I got sent to your company…
It wasn't a coincidence.

01:12:41.065 --> 01:12:44.360
My supervising attorney knew
we were classmates and sent me on purpose.

01:12:48.281 --> 01:12:51.951
Well, it's all in the past now,

01:12:52.034 --> 01:12:53.786
and you didn't know either.

01:12:55.872 --> 01:12:58.457
Even if you didn't drop the case
just because of me,

01:12:59.041 --> 01:13:02.295
since I was sent with that intention,
I still feel responsible.

01:13:04.463 --> 01:13:06.382
What's done is done,

01:13:06.966 --> 01:13:11.012
but if you ever need help,
I'll do whatever I can.

01:13:15.641 --> 01:13:18.311
Is that why you called me
all the way out here?

01:13:18.394 --> 01:13:20.688
Don't you need to go back to work?

01:13:22.398 --> 01:13:23.482
[sighs]

01:13:24.066 --> 01:13:25.568
I'm done for today.

01:13:26.611 --> 01:13:27.778
Thanks to you.

01:13:28.905 --> 01:13:30.239
What do you mean?

01:13:35.745 --> 01:13:36.787
Uh…

01:13:37.830 --> 01:13:39.206
Honestly…

01:13:40.833 --> 01:13:42.251
sometimes this job

01:13:43.002 --> 01:13:45.171
made me feel uneasy.

01:13:47.131 --> 01:13:50.217
And every time I felt uneasy,
I thought I was in the wrong.

01:13:50.301 --> 01:13:52.011
So I kept trying to change myself.

01:13:52.887 --> 01:13:54.221
But you said…

01:13:55.014 --> 01:13:57.767
when something gets stuck in my mind,

01:13:57.850 --> 01:14:00.144
I act like a kid
with a pebble in his shoe.

01:14:01.354 --> 01:14:02.688
That's when I realized.

01:14:03.898 --> 01:14:04.941
Well…

01:14:06.400 --> 01:14:09.695
I wasn't wrong.
I'd just forgotten who I was.

01:14:11.030 --> 01:14:13.074
[tender music playing]

01:14:13.658 --> 01:14:15.493
Sounds ridiculous, right?

01:14:17.495 --> 01:14:19.705
How do you forget yourself?

01:14:21.332 --> 01:14:23.542
But I did. All this time.

01:14:26.212 --> 01:14:27.421
So now,

01:14:28.214 --> 01:14:30.508
I'm going to start retracing my steps.

01:14:32.218 --> 01:14:33.678
See what else I've forgotten.

01:14:36.305 --> 01:14:39.308
[Mi-ji] Some people revisit the test
they got a perfect score on.

01:14:39.392 --> 01:14:40.476
[sighs]

01:14:40.559 --> 01:14:43.604
[Mi-ji] All this time,
I thought I knew myself and Mi-rae,

01:14:43.688 --> 01:14:47.316
but I was just guessing,
fooling myself into thinking I knew.

01:14:48.401 --> 01:14:51.821
There's more to it
than just getting the right answer.

01:14:56.033 --> 01:14:57.118
[knocking on door]

01:15:05.918 --> 01:15:08.796
CHANGHWA FARM
YIELD INCREASE PLAN AND ANNUAL SCHEDULE

01:15:12.842 --> 01:15:16.345
[Mi-ji] You only truly understand
some things after getting them wrong.

01:15:19.807 --> 01:15:22.268
Now that I know what I got wrong,

01:15:22.977 --> 01:15:26.188
maybe someday I'll get it right.

01:15:30.609 --> 01:15:31.736
What?

01:15:33.779 --> 01:15:35.823
- Nothing.
- [music concludes]

01:15:35.906 --> 01:15:38.617
I was wondering if I'd get better

01:15:38.701 --> 01:15:40.536
if I reviewed my mistakes.

01:15:43.205 --> 01:15:44.832
[cell phone buzzing]

01:15:48.669 --> 01:15:50.004
Hello?

01:15:50.087 --> 01:15:52.006
[Ro-sa] Be here by ten o'clock tomorrow.

01:15:52.089 --> 01:15:53.090
Pardon?

01:15:53.799 --> 01:15:56.886
You want to be treated like a person?
Then be here by 10:00.

01:15:57.928 --> 01:15:59.055
[receiver clatters]

01:16:04.185 --> 01:16:05.269
[gasps]

01:16:10.232 --> 01:16:11.609
Did something good happen?

01:16:12.610 --> 01:16:13.736
What?

01:16:14.361 --> 01:16:17.490
No, I'm not sure yet.

01:16:18.157 --> 01:16:20.785
Gosh, the Hangang River is amazing.

01:16:21.535 --> 01:16:24.288
Aren't you hungry?
Want to get some ramyun?

01:16:24.371 --> 01:16:26.540
Wait, what time's the fountain show?

01:16:26.624 --> 01:16:28.167
Should we eat after watching it?

01:16:28.250 --> 01:16:30.836
No, maybe we should wait until sunset…

01:16:30.920 --> 01:16:32.088
Mi-ji.

01:16:43.307 --> 01:16:44.642
You're Mi-ji, aren't you?

01:16:46.018 --> 01:16:48.479
[uplifting song playing]

01:16:48.562 --> 01:16:54.485
[singing in Korean]

01:16:54.568 --> 01:16:59.907
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:00.533 --> 01:17:05.454
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:06.497 --> 01:17:11.043
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:13.546 --> 01:17:19.135
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:19.301 --> 01:17:23.556
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:25.349 --> 01:17:30.104
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:30.980 --> 01:17:35.943
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:37.278 --> 01:17:40.197
[singing in Korean continues]

01:17:41.115 --> 01:17:42.283
YU MI-JI

01:17:42.366 --> 01:17:44.785
[worker] When did you do this?
You've pulled yourself together.

01:17:44.869 --> 01:17:45.828
[Se-jin] Right.

01:17:45.911 --> 01:17:47.955
Why are you playing so hard to get?

01:17:48.038 --> 01:17:49.999
That's enough. She said it's fine.

01:17:50.082 --> 01:17:51.834
[Mi-ji] Do you have a lawyer mode?

01:17:51.917 --> 01:17:54.545
- What?
- You should keep talking like that.

01:17:54.628 --> 01:17:55.629
It's cool.

01:17:55.713 --> 01:17:56.839
[Ho-su] Over here.

01:17:56.922 --> 01:17:57.882
[woman] Mi-rae.

01:17:57.965 --> 01:18:00.426
It's been such a long time.
How have you been?

01:18:00.509 --> 01:18:02.136
Oh. Hey, Ji-yun.

01:18:02.219 --> 01:18:04.221
How about a meeting
with the owner next week?

01:18:04.305 --> 01:18:05.222
Pardon?

01:18:05.306 --> 01:18:06.640
[Mi-ji] This is my specialty.

01:18:06.724 --> 01:18:08.601
[Ro-sa] What are you doing?

01:18:08.684 --> 01:18:11.812
Don't ever come back here.
I'm not selling my land.

01:18:12.521 --> 01:18:17.193
[singing continues in Korean]

01:18:18.054 --> 01:18:20.054
Subtitle translation by Soya Back
